## SQ-LBS-01 | labels by surface: face Place per host (zlbs labels)
@group A
@commands `/cltest surface` part `labels`: place `supplementaries:jar`, `supplementaries:sack`, the four `trashcans:*_trash_can`, `vintagedelight:fermenting_jar`, `botanypots:terracotta_botany_pot`, `minecraft:cauldron`, `minecraft:composter`, `minecraft:stone`, `minecraft:chest`; a label on each north side
@pass `[cltest] PASS` per host; face values: jar 0.1875/0/0/10, sack 0.125/0/-1/10, trash cans 0.125/0/0/10, Pickling Jar 0.203/0/0/10, botany pot 0.125/0/-4/8, cauldron and composter 0/0/0/10, stone 0/0/0/10, chest 0.0625/0/0/10
@fails `Spots.labelSurface` (headless `SpotsTest` "labels: surface test" passes, so the live shape differs: log `host.getShape` boxes) or `placeLabel` not reached (sneak needed on usable hosts)
@from batches/r1103/sB_2.qb
> zlbs labels
waitlog \[zlbs\] DONE labels 60
count \[zlbs\] PASS labels == 12
reject \[zlbs\] FAIL
look on a FAIL, the line's place (inset/offX/offY/size) against the wanted value; "labels left" 3 = one label used

